  "caption_en": "Numerical trajectories of the original SAPN at Q=400 for prespecified seed 23 on all five development corpora. Panel (a) divides each second-stage objective value by that stage's initial value; stage-one objectives are excluded because the orthogonality coefficient changes between stages. Panel (b) shows the maximum normalized block first-order residual on a logarithmic axis, with the 10^-3 stopping threshold. Points in (b) are the actual recorded checks; endpoints in (a) mark the recorded terminal iterations. These five runs required no continuation. Stopping additionally requires relative objective change below 10^-5. The curves illustrate finite numerical behavior and do not establish factor convergence or global optimality.",
  "transformations": [
    "Use seed 23 for every corpus, never select a best seed.",
    "Exclude stage one and normalize only by J at stage-two iteration zero.",
    "Append only same-objective continuation, if present, after checking the boundary identity.",
    "Plot recorded residuals on a base-10 logarithmic scale; no smoothing or zero-flooring."
  ],
